# JMX Password Credentials Template - SAMPLE ONLY
#
# This is a template file showing the FORMAT of jmxremote.password.
# DO NOT use these example passwords - they are for demonstration only.
#
# ⚠️ SECURITY CRITICAL:
# 1. Copy this file to create your actual jmxremote.password (which is in .gitignore)
# 2. Replace the example passwords with STRONG, RANDOM passwords (minimum 16 characters)
# 3. Generate secure passwords with:
#    openssl rand -base64 32 | tr -d "=+/" | cut -c1-25
# 4. NEVER commit jmxremote.password to version control
# 5. Rotate credentials regularly (quarterly minimum)
# 6. Store in a secure secret manager (AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault, Azure Key Vault)
#
# Format: <username> <password>
# Each user corresponds to a role defined in jmxremote.access

# Example - monitorRole with STRONG password (min 16 chars)
# monitorRole  aBc1dEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStUv

# Example - controlRole with STRONG password (min 16 chars)  
# controlRole  xYz9AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrSt

#
# Setup Instructions:
#
# 1. Generate secure passwords:
#    MONITOR_PWD=$(openssl rand -base64 32 | tr -d "=+/" | cut -c1-25)
#    CONTROL_PWD=$(openssl rand -base64 32 | tr -d "=+/" | cut -c1-25)
#    echo "monitorRole  $MONITOR_PWD" > secrets/jmxremote.password
#    echo "controlRole  $CONTROL_PWD" >> secrets/jmxremote.password
#
# 2. Set proper permissions:
#    chmod 600 secrets/jmxremote.password
#
# 3. Store passwords in your secret manager:
#    - AWS: aws secretsmanager create-secret --name kafka-jmx-monitor --secret-string "$MONITOR_PWD"
#    - Vault: vault kv put secret/kafka/jmx monitor_password="$MONITOR_PWD"
#    - Environment: export JMX_MONITOR_PASSWORD="$MONITOR_PWD"
#
# 4. During deployment, read from secret manager and inject:
#    docker run -e KEYSTORE_PASSWORD="$KS_PWD" -v $(pwd)/secrets:/etc/secrets:ro ...
#
# 5. Remove plaintext passwords after deployment:
#    shred -vfz -n 5 secrets/jmxremote.password
#
# Role Mapping:
# - monitorRole (read-only): Used by Grafana, Prometheus exporters, OpenTelemetry agents
# - controlRole (write-restricted): Used by Kafka operators and automation scripts
#
# See secrets/README.md and JMX_SECURITY_HARDENING.md for complete documentation.
